DexSwapModule::execute
├── when params are too short
│   ├── it should return failed result with invalid params encoding
│   └── it should not transfer any tokens
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should return failed result with zero sell amount
├── when target token is zero address
│   └── it should return failed result with zero target token
├── when target token equals sell token
│   └── it should return failed result with same input and output token
├── when maxSlippageBps is zero
│   └── it should return failed result with invalid slippage bps
├── when maxSlippageBps exceeds 10000
│   └── it should return failed result with invalid slippage bps
├── when sell token price feed is zero address
│   └── it should return failed result with missing sell token price feed
├── when buy token price feed is zero address
│   └── it should return failed result with missing buy token price feed
├── when swap deadline seconds is zero
│   └── it should return failed result with zero swap deadline
├── when caller has insufficient balance
│   └── it should return failed result with insufficient balance
├── when oracle price is unavailable (negative, stale, or reverts)
│   └── it should return failed result with oracle price unavailable
├── when router call reverts
│   ├── it should return failed result with router call failed
│   ├── it should return all sell tokens to caller via leftover
│   └── it should leave module with zero sell token balance
├── when router output is below oracle floor
│   ├── it should revert with DexSwapModule_InsufficientOutput
│   └── it should not transfer sell tokens (atomic rollback)
├── when router sends no buy tokens
│   └── it should revert atomically
├── when fee-on-transfer sell token
│   └── it should use balance-diff for actual received amount
├── when router partially consumes sell token
│   ├── it should succeed if output meets oracle floor
│   └── it should return unconsumed sell tokens to caller
├── when all validations pass
│   ├── it should transfer sell tokens from caller to router
│   ├── it should increase caller buy token balance by amountOut
│   ├── it should return success true
│   ├── it should return correct amountOut
│   ├── it should return outputToken equal to target token
│   ├── it should return empty data field
│   ├── it should emit SwapExecuted with correct params
│   ├── it should leave module with zero sell token balance
│   ├── it should leave module with zero buy token balance
│   ├── it should revoke router approval after swap
│   └── it should not hold any residual state between swaps
├── when router re-enters execute during swap callback
│   ├── it should revert the reentrant call with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall
│   ├── it should complete the original swap successfully
│   ├── it should leave attacker balances unchanged
│   └── it should allow subsequent swaps after blocked reentrancy
└── fuzz
    └── it should handle any valid sell amount and buy amount
